        "id": "intro",
        "type": "nodetool.workflows.base_node.Comment",
        "data": {
          "comment": "# Shot Director (Wan 2.2 14B)\n\nDirect a cinematic take from one still as a native ComfyUI graph on Comfy Cloud (Wan 2.2 I2V A14B with 4-step lightx2v, open weights). The same graph runs behind the Storyboard clip model \"Wan 2.2 I2V A14B (ComfyUI workflow, open weights)\".\n\n**How it works:** Run submits this graph to Comfy Cloud and saves the take. Set the still on the Load Image node and describe the shot in the prompt.\n\n**Camera moves:** Add one of these clauses to the end of the prompt.\n\n- **dolly in:** The camera glides forward toward the subject in one continuous movement. Nearby objects slide past faster than the distant background as the subject grows larger. One continuous shot.\n- **orbit:** The camera circles all the way around the subject at a steady height and distance, revealing front, side, back and front again in a continuous shot. One continuous shot.\n- **crane up:** The camera lifts above the subject and gradually points downward. More of the surrounding ground becomes visible as the subject recedes below. One continuous shot.\n- **pull back reveal:** Beginning close to the subject, the camera retreats smoothly into a wide shot. Surrounding scenery progressively enters at the edges and reveals the larger setting. One continuous shot.\n- **handheld:** Small irregular camera movements drift gently up, down and sideways, like a person holding a camera while standing still. The subject remains clearly visible. One continuous shot.\n- **static:** The camera holds exactly the same viewpoint and framing throughout the shot. Motion belongs to the subject and the environment inside the stationary frame. One continuous shot."
        },
